00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:42,340
This is maybe one of the best vanilla flavors

371
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:44,640
you will ever have ever.

372
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:48,040
Part of what makes ice cream mix at this stage so delicious

373
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:51,720
is how creamy it is, which reminds me of another frozen

374
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:54,420
treat that we all know and love.

375
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:59,260
We can't talk about ice cream without talking about...

376
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:01,260
Soft Serve.

377
00:18:01,261 --> 00:18:06,800
Soft Serve has less milk fat and more air than hard ice cream.

378
00:18:06,801 --> 00:18:12,440
You can't buy it at a supermarket because it takes a special machine to keep Soft Serve

379
00:18:12,441 --> 00:18:15,600
at a low but not completely frozen temperature.

380
00:18:15,601 --> 00:18:23,360
Soft Serve wasn't invented until the 1930s, and as soon as it was, America fell in love

381
00:18:23,361 --> 00:18:24,360
with it.

382
00:18:24,361 --> 00:18:25,360
Fast.

383
00:18:25,361 --> 00:18:29,660
By the 1950s, soft serve was outselling hard ice cream.

384
00:18:29,760 --> 00:18:32,600
An estimated 150 million gallons of it

385
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:35,500
was consumed in 1957 alone.

386
00:18:35,600 --> 00:18:38,500
But here is where it gets even more interesting.

387
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:41,600
The origins of soft serve are hotly debated,

388
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,940
and this ice cream battle royale involves two names

389
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:48,980
you just may have heard of, Dairy Queen and Carvel.

390
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:52,680
Dairy Queen founder J.F. McCullough first sold ice cream

391
00:18:52,681 --> 00:18:57,820
sold ice cream in its softer pre-hardened state in 1938.

392
00:18:57,821 --> 00:19:01,820
He sold 1,600 servings of his new product

393
00:19:01,821 --> 00:19:05,860
in less than two hours the first day he offered it.

394
00:19:05,861 --> 00:19:10,220
But it took several years before McCuller perfected a freezer

395
00:19:10,221 --> 00:19:13,040
that reliably dispensed soft serve.

396
00:19:13,041 --> 00:19:15,040
It was actually based off a machine

397
00:19:15,041 --> 00:19:19,560
used for frozen custard, which is neither ice cream nor soft

398
00:19:19,561 --> 00:19:20,261
serve.

399
00:19:20,262 --> 00:19:22,240
Frozen custard, by legal definition,

400
00:19:22,241 --> 00:19:25,960
has to have 1.4% or more egg yolk.

401
00:19:25,961 --> 00:19:29,040
People love custard because the egg yolk gives it

402
00:19:29,041 --> 00:19:31,000
a more robust texture.

403
00:19:31,001 --> 00:19:33,800
Meanwhile, Carvel founder Tom Carvel

404
00:19:33,801 --> 00:19:36,960
hit upon the idea for soft serve when his freezer truck

405
00:19:36,961 --> 00:19:39,700
broke down in 1934.

406
00:19:39,701 --> 00:19:42,760
Realizing his product would soon literally melt away,

407
00:19:42,761 --> 00:19:46,060
Tom quickly started selling it to anyone and everyone who

408
00:19:46,061 --> 00:19:48,340
stopped by and was surprised to find

409
00:19:48,341 --> 00:19:52,340
loved the melty softer version of his ice cream.

410
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:57,340
The rest is soft serve history.

411
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:05,340
Today, we're going behind the curtain at Carvel in Hackensack, New Jersey.

412
00:20:05,341 --> 00:20:13,340
Since 1974, this location has been run by a husband and wife team who trained under Tom Carvel himself.

413
00:20:13,341 --> 00:20:15,000
Hi, what can I get for you?

414
00:20:15,001 --> 00:20:16,180
Oh, yeah.

415
00:20:16,181 --> 00:20:17,680
That customer walks in the door,

416
00:20:17,681 --> 00:20:21,340
they have 100% of your attention.

417
00:20:21,341 --> 00:20:24,380
While Tom Sasso was training under Tom Carvell,

418
00:20:24,381 --> 00:20:26,180
the company's founder and namesake

419
00:20:26,181 --> 00:20:28,380
was working on a new idea.

420
00:20:28,381 --> 00:20:30,500
Ice cream cakes had existed in America

421
00:20:30,501 --> 00:20:33,000
since at least the 19th century.

422
00:20:33,001 --> 00:20:35,500
Tom Carvell's revolutionary concept

423
00:20:35,501 --> 00:20:38,400
was to create themed ice cream cakes

424
00:20:38,401 --> 00:20:40,140
using signature ingredients,

425
00:20:40,141 --> 00:20:43,340
and then tie them to particular holidays.

426
00:20:43,341 --> 00:20:47,040
Carvel's most iconic cake was launched in 1977

427
00:20:47,041 --> 00:20:50,340
to celebrate a whale of a dad on Father's Day,

428
00:20:50,341 --> 00:20:51,880
Fudgy the Whale.

429
00:20:51,881 --> 00:20:55,780
His homemade commercials for it quickly became a sensation.

430
00:20:55,781 --> 00:20:57,580
It was Tom's voice.

431
00:20:57,581 --> 00:21:01,800
It was a gravelly voice that you either loved or you hated.

432
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:05,500
Fudgy the Whale is back.

